From: Steamac maintainers <steamac@fxgam.es>
Subject: [PATCH] SPIRV-Cross: adapt physical raster vector widths without truncation

Honor caller-proven ordinary vertex/fragment vector widths with an opt-in pad_stage_interface_components option. Keep the shader logical type intact and widen only the Metal interface member. Copy every producer-written lane, zero only absent lanes, and swizzle the physical fragment input back to the logical width.

Handle plain, array/matrix-flattened and interface-block members while retaining location/component and interpolation decorations. Exact location/component lookup only; no vertex-fetch fallback and no tessellation/geometry buffer ABI changes.

Historical STEAMAC-2M/88 float3/float4 signatures motivated this change. Verification delegated to the integrating parent; no builds or tests run here.

